<% content_for :title, "Roles on Fuime" %>

<div class="overview">
  <h2>Overview</h2>
  <p>
    Every person on a Fuime business has a role, and the role decides what they
    can do. When you invite someone, you pick their role &mdash; and you can
    change it later.
  </p>

  <p>There are three:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Owners</strong> run the business. They can do everything: spend,
      invite people, change settings.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Team members</strong> work in the business. They can <em>spend</em>,
      but not <em>send</em> money, and they can't change the business's settings.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Parents</strong> can see everything and change nothing. This is the
      seat for a parent or guardian who wants to keep an eye on the money.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <%= render "application/callout", type: "info", title: "Parents and guardians" do %>
    <p class="m0">
      The <strong>Parent</strong> role is a view of the business, not the legal
      guardianship itself. If you're under 18, your parent or guardian signs for
      your account separately &mdash; that's what actually lets you operate a
      business on Fuime, and it's set up from your account settings.
    </p>
  <% end %>

  <h2>Detailed breakdown</h2>

  <div class="overflow-x-auto p2">
    <table>
      <tr style="border-bottom-width: 3px">
        <th></th>
        <% OrganizerPosition.roles.keys.each do |role| %>
          <th><%= role_label(role).pluralize %></th>
        <% end %>
      </tr>
      <%= render_permissions(@perms) %>
    </table>
  </div>
</div>
